{title: In Remembrance of Me}
{subtitle: Matthew 26:17–30; 1 Corinthians 11:23–26; Luke 22:14–20; John 13:1–15}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Ab/Eb] [Eb] | [Bb7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Upon the night he was betrayed
[Ab]Within [Eb]the upper room
The Lord sat down [Cm]among his friends
[Bb]Beneath [Eb]the gathering [Ab]gloom
He took a [Bb]basin and [Gm]a towel
And knelt [Cm]upon [Ab]the floor
The Teacher and the Lord [Bb]of all
Washed feet and asked no more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]This is my body, [Ab]which is [Bb]for you
Do this in re[Eb]membrance of me
This cup is the new covenant [Ab]in my [Bb]blood
Do this in remem[Eb]brance of me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He took the bread and gave God thanks
And [Ab]broke it, [Eb]saying, Take
He passed the cup of covenant
Poured [Bb]out for [Eb]sinners' sake
I [Ab]will not drink this fruit [Bb]again
[Gm]He told the twelve [Cm]that night
[Ab]Until I drink it new with you
In [Bb]my Father's kingdom bright
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
This is my [Eb]body, which is for [Ab]you
Do [Bb]this in remembrance of [Eb]me
This cup is the new covenant in my blood
[Ab]Do this [Bb]in remembrance of me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]As of[Cm]ten as you eat [Bb]this bread and drink [Ab]this cup
[Eb]You [Cm]proclaim the Lord's [Bb]death until [Ab]he comes
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]They sang a hymn and rose to go
Out to the o[Ab]live hill
[Eb]The Lamb walked out into the night
To do his Fa[Bb]ther's will
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]This is my body, which is for you
Do [Ab]this in [Bb]remembrance of me
This [Eb]cup is the new covenant in my blood
Do this [Ab]in re[Bb]membrance of me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Do [Eb]this in [Bb]remembrance of [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}
